public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String productName = "Laptop";
        int productID = 101;
        double price = 45999.99;
        boolean availability = true;

        System.out.println("***************************");
        System.out.println("       PRODUCT CARD        ");
        System.out.println("***************************");
        System.out.println("Product Name : " + productName);
        System.out.println("Product ID   : " + productID);
        System.out.println("Price        : Rs. " + price);
        System.out.println("Availability : " + availability);
        System.out.println("***************************");
    }
}
Output
text
***************************
       PRODUCT CARD
***************************
Product Name : Laptop
Product ID   : 101
Price        : Rs. 45999.99
Availability : true
***************************
Explanation
String — stores the product name.

int — stores the product ID.

double — stores the product price.

boolean — stores availability (true or false).

System.out.println() — displays each detail on a separate line.


